  "independent_work": "Package-10 replaces uniform orange damage tint with dark coated steel and localized first/latest hit marks. Eleven native methods and all damage gameplay bytes remain identical to package-09 after excluding material bindings. Saved material readback, native/editor builds, cook/archive/install and installed environment checks pass. The 720p ordinary-input run ended in native Success after 13.70411386800697 active seconds and 13 input actions, recording one bay power transition with no panel damage or electrical-floor damage. Its inspected 12-second and 15-second video frames show approach to the bay and unbroken dark panels beside the abrupt wet-floor edge; they do not show a damaged panel. The 1080p run ended in native Success after 8.804244222992565 active seconds and five input actions, with no bay power, panel or electrical-floor events. Its four-second frame shows the blue player, yellow rival and red infected on a sparse flat road with placeholder focal geometry and oversized HUD panels. Both runs contain native combat events, zero restarts and no captured audio; neither establishes the long-form route or full evolving arena consequence. Soften the abrupt service-bay wet-floor boundary into the surrounding road using the existing ground material; preserve geometry, collision and hazard rules, then inspect the transition in packaged gameplay.",
